  "term": "Conners’ Comprehensive Behavior Rating Scales",
  "definition": "Conners’ Comprehensive Behavior Rating Scales refers to a set of behavior rating scales used in this source to assess children’s behavioral and emotional problems. In the preschool sample described, it included areas such as hyperactivity, learning problems, conduct problems, anxiety, and psychosomatic problems.",
